***************************
* SET UP THE INITIAL DATA *
***************************

NAME          GBRAINLS

*   Problem :
*   *********

*   Match a model of the shear moduli in the human brain to data,
*   formulated as a nonlinear least-squares problem

*   Source: an example in
*   L.A. Mihai, S. Budday, G.A. Holzapfel, E. Kuhl and A. Goriely.
*   "A family of hyperelastic models for human brain tissue",
*   Journal of Mechanics and Physics of Solids,
*   DOI: 10.1016/j.jmps.2017.05.015 (2017).

*   as conveyed by Angela Mihai (U. Cardiff)

*   SIF input: Nick Gould, June 2017.

*   classification SUR2-MN-2-0

*   N is the number of data sets

 IE N                   11

*   M is the number of discretizations

 IE M                   200

*   Define useful parameters

 IE 0                   0
 IE 1                   1

VARIABLES

    ALPHA
    C0

GROUPS

 DO J         1                        N
 DO I         1                        M
 XN R(I,J)
 ND

CONSTANTS

